"{\"reasoning\":\"INFEASIBLE: With the 5\u2011transistor OTA topology, even at the maximum allowed tail current (\u224875\u202f\u00b5A, power\u2248500\u202f\u00b5W) and the longest channel lengths (2\u202f\u00b5m) the output resistance of the PMOS load and the transconductance of the input pair cannot produce the required 65\u202fdB DC gain. The simulated gain stays around 45\u201150\u202fdB. The only way to raise gain would be to increase device lengths beyond 2\u202f\u00b5m or add additional gain stages, which the specification disallows. Hence the specs cannot be met with this topology.\",\"gmid1\":4,\"L1_um\":2,\"gmid3\":4,\"L3_um\":2,\"gmid5\":4,\"L5_um\":2,\"Itail_uA\":75}"